---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../site/config';
---

<Base
  title="Hermes Agent"
  description="Hermes Agent is a private, single-user automation agent that runs on its owner's own computer."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Hermes Agent', path: '/hermes' }]}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <header>
      <p class="legal-page__eyebrow">Software</p>
      <h1>Hermes Agent</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated 21 October 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="legal-page__content">
      <p>
        Hermes Agent is a private, single-user software agent. It is not a product, has no sign-up,
        and is not offered to the public. It runs locally on my own laptop in Wellington, New
        Zealand, and acts only on my behalf and only on my own accounts and devices.
      </p>

      <section aria-labelledby="what-it-does">
        <h2 id="what-it-does">What it does</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Reads and drafts email, and sends messages I have asked it to send.</li>
          <li>Reads my calendar and creates or moves events when I ask.</li>
          <li>Reads and writes my own documents, spreadsheets and task lists.</li>
          <li>Keeps a local, private record of my finances from data I already have access to.</li>
          <li>Runs scheduled reminders and summaries for me.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works">
        <h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
        <p>
          The agent runs on the same machine I use and stores its working data there. It talks to
          Google services through the OAuth grant I give it myself, and only for the scopes I
          approve on the consent screen. It is not a hosted service, has no servers of its own
          holding user data, and no third party is given access to anything it can see.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy">
        <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          What it can see, where that data is stored, and how to withdraw access are described in
          the <a href="/hermes/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contact">
        <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Owner and sole user: Hamish Burke, Wellington, New Zealand.
          Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
